      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-10T18:43:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we standardize and use `std::string` here? I get that this avoids a `UTF8ToWStr` conversion, and it also Windows-only, so probably okay?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "a4fdb6c078ebd29ea6371f52a17ca1643b842eed",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93e22de6_1e7e30e3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/common/DynamicLib.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000262
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-10T19:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The implementation of `LoadLibraryExA` converts the passed in string to wide characters and calls `LoadLibraryExW`. So having this method accept `std::string` means two string conversions, one when calling \"OpenSystemLibrary\" and one when calling the OS. Passing a `std::wstring_view` here eliminates both the copies.\n\nAs a followon change, would be good for us to standardize on wide characters for all of the Windows filepath ingesting code in Dawn. FWIW, Chromium does this.",
      "parentUuid": "21028785_d36bb4f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "a4fdb6c078ebd29ea6371f52a17ca1643b842eed",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b57d26a_9bf7a3bd",
        "filename": "src/dawn/common/DynamicLib.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-11T08:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TBH this code is so cold that it either way is probably fine.\n\n\u003e As a followon change, would be good for us to standardize on wide characters for all of the Windows filepath ingesting code in Dawn. FWIW, Chromium does this.\n\nDo you mean on all platforms? How is that efficient on non-Windows? (but also Dawn basically opens no files so it really doesn\u0027t seem important to do)",
      "parentUuid": "93e22de6_1e7e30e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 27,
